
  LRC AS CIRCULAR-ARC COVERING: THE DEPTH DISTRIBUTION p_k

======================================================================

  I. FIRST-MOMENT LAW  sum_k k p_k = 2 n delta = 2n/(n+1)
  --------------------------------------------------
  V                       sum k p_k   2n/(n+1)   match
  (1, 2, 3)                     3/2        3/2    True
  (1, 3, 4, 7)                  8/5        8/5    True
  (1, 3, 4, 5, 9)               5/3        5/3    True
  (1, 2, 4)                     3/2        3/2    True
  (1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 11, 13)        7/4        7/4    True
  (exact; each forbidden set has measure 2*delta, so the mean depth is
   fixed at 2n/(n+1) for ALL speed sets -- only the SHAPE of p_k varies.)

  II. THE LONELINESS FUNCTIONAL  Lambda(V) = p_0;  tight <=> p_0 = 0
  --------------------------------------------------
  V                             p_0  tight? (extremal: delta_max = 1/(n+1))
  (1, 2, 3, 4)                    0    True
  (1, 3, 4, 7)                    0    True
  (1, 2, 4)                     1/8   False
  (1, 2, 3, 5)                 4/75   False
  (1, 3, 4, 5, 9)                 0    True
  (1, 3, 4, 9, 10, 12)         1/18   False
  (p_0 = 0 means the forbidden arcs cover the circle up to measure zero:
   the lonely set is a finite set of witness points -- the EXTREMAL case.)

  III. DEPTH-DISTRIBUTION ENTROPY = ORDER PARAMETER FOR TIGHTNESS
  --------------------------------------------------
  Same mean (2n/(n+1)) for all; tight configs MINIMIZE the entropy H(p).
  V                         tight    H(p)  profile p_0 p_1 p_2 ...
  (1, 2, 3, 4)               True   0.972  0.00 0.63 0.23 0.03 0.10
  (1, 3, 4, 7)               True   1.028  0.00 0.62 0.21 0.11 0.06
  (1, 2, 3, 5)              False   1.222  0.05 0.51 0.31 0.05 0.08
  (1, 2, 3, 4, 5)            True   1.018  0.00 0.59 0.29 0.03 0.02 0.07
  (1, 3, 4, 5, 9)            True   1.088  0.00 0.57 0.30 0.07 0.03 0.04
  (1, 3, 4, 7, 11)          False   1.305  0.05 0.47 0.34 0.08 0.04 0.03
  (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6)         True   1.090  0.00 0.60 0.25 0.07 0.01 0.01 0.05
  (1, 3, 4, 9, 10, 12)      False   1.309  0.06 0.46 0.29 0.17 0.00 0.00 0.02
  (at each n: tight H < non-tight H; the AP is the global entropy min --
   tightness = the entropy-minimal / most efficient circular cover.)

  IV. THE COLLAPSE FAMILY: additive-chain NECESSARY, not sufficient
  --------------------------------------------------
  Exhaustive census of primitive (gcd=1) speed sets:
    n    B  #tight  all chains?  #chains  tight/chains
    4   20       2         True       62          2/62
    5   20       2         True      110         2/110
    6   20       1         True      257         1/257
  Tight sets found (chain-only search, B<=30):
    n=4: (1, 2, 3, 4)[AP], (1, 3, 4, 7)[sporadic]
    n=5: (1, 2, 3, 4, 5)[AP], (1, 3, 4, 5, 9)[sporadic]
    n=6: (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6)[AP]
    n=7: (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)[AP], (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 12)[sporadic], (1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 11, 13)[sporadic]

  V. NEGATIVE RESULTS: the natural patterns are COINCIDENCES
  --------------------------------------------------
  Lucas chain (1,3,4,7,11,18,...):
    (1, 3, 4, 7)           tight=True
    (1, 3, 4, 7, 11)       tight=False
    (1, 3, 4, 7, 11, 18)   tight=False
  Paley QR mod p  (these are NOT a tight family):
    p= 7 QR=(1, 2, 4)                    tight=False
    p=11 QR=(1, 3, 4, 5, 9)              tight=True
    p=13 QR=(1, 3, 4, 9, 10, 12)         tight=False
    p=17 QR=(1, 2, 4, 8, 9, 13, 15, 16)  tight=False
    p=19 QR=(1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 11, 16, 17) tight=False
  => (1,3,4,7)=Lucas and (1,3,4,5,9)=QR mod 11 are isolated coincidences,
     NOT instances of a Lucas-tight or Paley-tight family. The collapse
     family is genuinely sporadic beyond the AP.

  VI. TIE TO THE RECURSIVE-LOG / HELLY-ENTROPY FRAME (HYP-2151)
  --------------------------------------------------
  p_0 = 0 is the Helly-INFEASIBLE boundary: the forbidden arcs cover, so no
  positive-measure lonely point exists (only measure-zero witnesses survive).
  The depth distribution p_k is the covering MULTIPLICITY profile that a binary
  Helly test (feasible? / cover?) collapses to one bit; H(p) is its entropy
  refinement. In the rank language of HYP-2151: a tight cover spends its arc
  measure with minimal entropy (rank-economical), the AP being the extreme.
  The loneliness functional Lambda=p_0 is the continuous order parameter whose
  zero set is the collapse family -- the LRC analogue of 'exact cover'.

======================================================================
  SUMMARY
  -------
  * LRC at gap delta = circular-arc covering; master object = depth distn p_k.
  * First-moment law (proved): mean depth = 2n/(n+1), fixed for all V.
  * Lonely measure Lambda = p_0; tight (extremal) <=> p_0 = 0.
  * Depth-entropy H(p) is the order parameter: tight configs minimize it
    (AP = global min); non-tight pay entropy for wasted lonely measure.
  * Collapse family: additive-chain NECESSARY (exhaustive n<=6) but far from
    sufficient; AP universal; sporadics rare; Lucas/Paley are coincidences.
  NEW SUB-PROBLEM (open): characterize the sporadic tight chains. Conjecture:
  tight => additive chain; refine by the witness lattice / depth-entropy.

